    "body": "Cause found. The extended Outside band on Milling-test is an annulus 14 mm wide (outline grown ~14 mm) for a D10 tool, so the legal centre area is a closed channel ~4 mm wide and ~275 mm long. It is not a star cell, so the planner takes the growth-ring path (adaptive/grow.rs): the hole is slit open and ONE spiral grows along the C-shaped channel. In a 4 mm channel each revolution holds the load at a step of only 0.12-0.37 mm (~1.1-2 mm^2 of centre area per revolution out of ~1100 mm^2), while every revolution rides and re-walks the whole cleared outline (ring 250-500 vertices, up to 7 step trials each on a 1.3 M-cell planner raster). Release timing: margin scale 1.0 ran 140 revs in 9.8 s and returned Short at 223 mm^2; scale 1.6 likewise (~224 revs); scale 2.4 is uncapped by the margin and runs toward MAX_REVS 800 with ever-longer rings - roughly a minute in release, many minutes in debug. Work grows ~ L^2/(step*w) with the channel length, so the 14x60 slot fixture is fast and this 5x longer channel is not. Fix in progress: a scale-free work budget on the growth plan (walked trial length per mm^2 of centre area, in optimal widths) that refuses it by name and hands the band to the Offset rings at once.",
