    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:00:28Z",
    "body": "Fix ready (staged in agent worktree, uncommitted, for the main session to commit). New `motion::machining2d::adaptive::budget`: (1) an up-front least-work law for the growth-ring spiral - channel length L = centre area / (2 x entry clearance), fronts each travelling L/2 at most the 1.5-width step cap a revolution over rings averaging L: L^2/(2 cap) tool radii, refused past 2000 r (60x14 slot ~110 r; the user's band ~3400 r); (2) a running net on the summed length of every revolution tried, all margin attempts, refused past 30 000 r (slot spends ~5800 r). A refused plan has no passes and pocket_hsm names it - 'the HSM plan is refused: the area is a channel 13.9 mm wide and ~269 mm long (the band round a part?) - one adaptive spiral would need at least 61 revolutions along it ... - Offset rings cut this pocket instead'. Timing on the band: was >6 min debug / ~1 min release (killed); now 0.06 s release, ~1 s debug. Pinned by motion adaptive_band (adaptive_on_an_annular_band_finishes_in_seconds, the_users_band_is_refused_by_name_up_front), budget unit test, and app shoulder_adaptive::containment_outside_clears_past_the_edge_never_the_recess now generating with 2D Adaptive (verifies clean, names the refusal). Gates: -Tier quick green, adaptive_hsm debug green, heavy hsm_report_full_resolution release green, clippy -D warnings clean on motion+app. Follow-up worth an issue if the adaptive is wanted on long bands: an incremental ring walk in grow (the real speed-up).",
